WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:05.651
There is a stunning new poll from right wing
Fox news showing that that

00:00:05.651 --> 00:00:12.700
more than half of Americans want Donald Trump,
not just impeached, but impeached and removed

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.700
from office.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.700
Now.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.640
Earlier this week I told you about the new
Washington post poll and that one said 60%

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:26.009
of the country agrees with the impeachment
inquiry and that support for the inquiry has

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:32.169
tripled among Republicans from about 10% to
about 30% the Fox news poll asked something

00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:38.790
else which is do you believe that Donald Trump
should be impeached and removed and 51% of

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:45.039
Americans now say yes, he should an additional
4% say yes on impeachment but not yet sure

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:46.329
on the removal.

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:51.460
This poll being from Fox news will likely
accelerate Donald Trump's breakup with Fox

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.769
news, which we've been tracking for a long
time.

00:00:53.769 --> 00:00:57.600
That's really kind of a sad store, a side
story, but there is one interesting thing

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.879
to mention there.

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:02.871
Remember how last week I told you that former
Republican speaker of the house, Paul Ryan

00:01:02.871 --> 00:01:05.439
is now a board member at Fox news.

00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:07.390
There is speculation.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.619
People are saying as Donald Trump likes to
say, there is speculation that it is Paul

00:01:11.619 --> 00:01:14.070
Ryan's disgust with Donald Trump.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:20.270
That may actually be behind some of the separation
that we're seeing between Fox and Trump recently,

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.360
which is an interesting theory, but a story
for another day.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.100
Back to the polling, truly devastating numbers,
and I want to talk about why and I really

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.390
want you to understand the significance of
these numbers.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.560
I went back and looked at polling from the
1970s Gallop was doing a lot of polling of

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.930
the Nixon white house in the 1970s this was
when the water date's scandal was ramping

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:48.759
up for Richard Nixon and the portion of the
country that wanted Nixon impeached remained

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:54.359
quite low, well into the impeachment inquiry
even when the majority of the country already

00:01:54.359 --> 00:01:57.270
believed Watergate is serious.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:03.369
Already believed that Nixon was guilty of
wrongdoing in that only 26% of the country

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:08.730
believed that Richard Nixon should be impeached
and removed and Nixon remember, didn't have

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:14.250
the benefit of a right wing media echo chamber
defending everything that he does all the

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.250
time.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:20.410
This thing started two weeks ago and more
than half of the country now believes that

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:25.050
the president should be removed from office
in a Fox news poll.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:28.710
Now there's another interesting thing for
most presidents.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:32.020
You gauge how things are going by approval
rating.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.440
Trump's approval rating has become completely
secondary.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.710
We are now gauging how things are going by
how many people want Donald Trump impeached

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:41.710
and removed.

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:42.860
This is not normal.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:48.800
The fact that the focus now is not on approval,
but on impeachment support means that things

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.250
are are very different from the way they normally
are with American presidents.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:58.290
This is also, by the way, new territory for
Trump in that in business, when he's gotten

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:03.580
into trouble, he has the escape hatch of bankruptcy
and he's used it.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.280
He's pulled, he's pulled the cord on that
escape hatch.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.881
Many times you can't declare bankruptcy from
what's going on right now.

00:03:09.881 --> 00:03:14.330
I guess the equivalent would be resignation,
but we're very, very far from that really

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.570
being a discussion.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:20.990
So that being said, a refusal to cooperate
with the impeachment inquiry makes him look

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:23.540
more guilty to normal people.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.360
His followers will resist that.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:27.440
They'll say, no, no, he's doing the right
thing.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.990
It's a witch hunt.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:29.990
He's fighting it.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:31.970
He's not going to bow down to the witch hunt.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:37.210
But even some Republicans are going to see
Trump's refusal to cooperate at all as a sign

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.210
of guilt.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.510
Nixon tried to fight impeachment.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:41.510
He lost.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:45.500
Trump, thinks he can fight it, and when he
may be right, a buddy may not.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:46.920
Now let me throw something else at you.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:51.000
About the 51% wanting Donald Trump impeached
and removed.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.260
Trump lost the popular vote.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.260
Okay.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.330
By a lot, by more than any previous president,
millions of votes.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:00.960
This is now being called a coup attempt by
defenders of Trump.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.140
And by Trump himself.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:07.960
This is a cue to reverse the election results
and remove Donald Trump from office by the

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:11.590
very people who never voted for him in the
first place.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:18.319
I went back and looked, every impeachment
in history was called a coup attempt by the

00:04:18.319 --> 00:04:21.290
defenders of the president that was at risk
of being removed.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:28.700
So that is another propaganda technique made
to once again, uh, distract from the fact.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.030
And I encourage you not to fall for it.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:37.400
This is a constitutionally enshrined mechanism
to investigate and adjudicate the wrongdoing

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.400
of a precedent.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.400
It is not a coup.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.409
It's almost the opposite and it is not a new
thing.

00:04:42.409 --> 00:04:47.599
Every president facing impeachment has had
defenders say, this is an attempt at a coup.

00:04:47.599 --> 00:04:49.000
It is not.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:49.180
This is how the system is designed.

